Subject: [PATCH] Limit setuptools package discovery to get_gecko_driver

Upstream's `[tool.setuptools.packages.find]` sets no `include` or `exclude`,
so automatic discovery picks up the top-level `tests` directory alongside
`get_gecko_driver`. The published wheel installs `tests/__init__.py` and
`tests/test_app.py` straight into site-packages, where they collide with
every other package that does the same thing.

--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -52,4 +52,5 @@
 
 [tool.setuptools.packages.find]
 where = [""]
+include = ["get_gecko_driver*"]
 namespaces = false
\ No newline at end of file
